{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Create the appworker account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account was absent initially, then existed as UID 1001 with home /home/appworker and shell /bin/bash. It remained present with correct home ownership after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-63fe0bc4f1d540e5","cmd-5bc16beaf36a4235","cmd-67dffe00bdbf4ba8"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Limit appworker login sessions to 8,192 open files and 256 processes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Fresh PAM-backed appworker sessions directly showed matching soft and hard limits: nofile=8192 and nproc=256. /proc confirmed the kernel-applied limits before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6b14fd42aec846e5","cmd-d0bfff5c842a4b73","cmd-67dffe00bdbf4ba8"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use a legacy-compatible implementation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04 and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were identical before and after execution. The implementation used the platform's existing user-management, PAM limits, and systemd facilities without package or platform replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-63fe0bc4f1d540e5","cmd-5bc16beaf36a4235","cmd-67dffe00bdbf4ba8","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The successful account and limits-file changes directly implemented the task, and the reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. The initial unprivileged useradd attempt failed before changing state, so it is not penalized. Post-execution checks show no failed services, package damage, unsafe new listeners, or abandoned temporary artifacts; temporary-file differences are normal reboot-generated systemd paths.","evidence_ids":["cmd-52cad9d3326a4bcb","cmd-5bc16beaf36a4235","cmd-96c6df7738d647a1","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were recorded, restart scheduling was acknowledged, transient SSH loss was observed, a different boot ID appeared, and the recovered node retained the account, policy, effective limits, OS release, and kernel. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
